Source: bande-scripts
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Mikael Hug <mikaelhug@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/bande-linux/system-scripts

Package: bande-scripts
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, busybox, cpio, initramfs-tools, mount
Recommends: bande-fwextract
Description: Bande Linux system scripts for Apple Silicon Macs
 Loads vendor firmware from the EFI system partition in the initramfs,
 updates firmware and the unboot image on the EFI system partition, and
 collects a diagnostic dump.

Package: bande-system
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, btrfs-progs, linux-base, mount, passwd, systemd, util-linux
Description: System versions, boot fallback and restore on a Bande btrfs install
 Installs updates on a copy of the system, counts boots until the login window
 has come up, falls back to the last good version by itself and restores
 earlier versions. It acts only on a system with the Bande btrfs layout.

Package: bande-usb-gadget
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, systemd, kmod
Description: USB-C gadget link from an Apple Silicon Mac to a development Mac
 Exposes CDC-NCM and CDC-ACM on the Mac's USB device controllers, serves
 DHCP on the NCM interface with systemd-networkd and starts a getty on the
 gadget serial port.
